### Usage Patterns

**Produces AlreadyExists error when:**
1. Creating a file exclusively with File::create_new() when file exists
2. Creating a directory with create_dir() when path exists
3. Creating directory tree with create_dir_all() when file blocks path

**Does NOT produce AlreadyExists:**
- File::create() (standard creation truncates existing files)

